WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.953
Henry ran as fast as he could. The woman was walking quickly.

2
00:00:18.954 --> 00:00:22.812
"There she goes—behind the restrooms!" Maggie said.

3
00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:25.427
"We might be able to trap her back there!"

4
00:00:25.428 --> 00:00:28.268
The Lemonade Detectives sped after her.

5
00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:32.698
When they rounded the corner, the woman had stopped to look at some flowers.

6
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.897
"Don't take another step!" Maggie cried.

7
00:00:35.898 --> 00:00:41.732
The woman looked startled. She backed away from them. "Who are you?"

8
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:47.096
Henry stepped forward. "We were about to ask you the same thing."

9
00:00:47.097 --> 00:00:51.567
His heart was pounding. They had to get the woman to confess!

10
00:00:51.568 --> 00:00:57.438
"Very funny," the woman snapped. "Now what do you want?"

11
00:00:57.439 --> 00:01:01.457
"We want you to give back our friend's painting," Cole said.

12
00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:04.550
The woman blinked. "What?"

13
00:01:04.551 --> 00:01:07.341
"Nathan's painting," Henry said.

14
00:01:07.342 --> 00:01:11.219
"We know you took it. Now tell us why you did it."

15
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:17.694
The woman shook her head, looking puzzled. "I didn't take anybody's painting."

16
00:01:17.695 --> 00:01:21.382
"Then why did you run away from us earlier?" Maggie demanded.

17
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.405
The woman peered at her.

18
00:01:23.406 --> 00:01:30.015
"Oh, was that you? I didn't get a good look at you then." She frowned.

19
00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:36.841
"Wait! Were you kids chasing me earlier because you thought I stole some painting?"

20
00:01:36.842 --> 00:01:39.302
"That's right," Henry said.

21
00:01:39.303 --> 00:01:42.039
The woman touched her bright red hair.

22
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.187
"So you weren't following me because you recognized me?"

23
00:01:46.188 --> 00:01:50.248
"Yes, we were!" Maggie crossed her arms over her chest.

24
00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:53.997
"We recognized you as an international art thief!"

25
00:01:53.998 --> 00:02:00.470
"Wait." Henry was listening carefully. "Why else would we recognize you?

26
00:02:00.471 --> 00:02:04.338
We already guessed you were from out of town, remember?"

27
00:02:04.339 --> 00:02:07.181
This time the woman turned to peer at Henry.

28
00:02:07.182 --> 00:02:10.685
"You did?" Suddenly she nodded.

29
00:02:10.686 --> 00:02:15.369
"Oh right. You're the kids from the lemonade stand!"

30
00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:19.396
"Yes," Cole said. "Who are you?"

31
00:02:19.397 --> 00:02:27.174
"Daniella Diaz, of course!" The woman paused, looking at each of the kids.

32
00:02:27.175 --> 00:02:30.452
"The world-famous artist?"

33
00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:33.172
Henry and the others looked at each other.

34
00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:39.434
Cole shrugged. "Sorry," he said. "I guess we don't know much about art."

35
00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:44.726
"Clearly." Daniella frowned. "Well, that's all right.

36
00:02:44.727 --> 00:02:48.865
I didn't want to be recognized today anyway.

37
00:02:48.866 --> 00:02:53.943
That's why I was trying to get out of sight when I saw the judges heading my way.

38
00:02:53.944 --> 00:02:59.460
I knew they'd spot me even in this wig." She patted her hair again.

39
00:02:59.461 --> 00:03:03.939
"That's a wig?" Maggie stared at it. "Wow."

40
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:11.247
"So if you're really a world-famous artist, what are you doing in Belltown?" Cole asked.

41
00:03:11.248 --> 00:03:13.560
"Yeah," Henry added.

42
00:03:13.561 --> 00:03:20.221
"And if you're a famous artist who doesn't want to be recognized, what are you doing at an art show?"

43
00:03:20.222 --> 00:03:24.274
"I'm visiting relatives in the area," Daniella replied.

44
00:03:24.275 --> 00:03:29.488
"I didn't know this art show was going on until I got here." She shrugged.

45
00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:34.030
"But once I heard about it, I couldn't resist coming to take a look.

46
00:03:34.031 --> 00:03:37.904
I wanted to check for small-town talent."

47
00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:44.741
"So you really didn't have anything to do with our friend's painting disappearing?" Henry asked.

48
00:03:44.742 --> 00:03:52.238
"Of course not." Daniella looked insulted. "I create art—I don't steal it."

49
00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:57.547
Henry nodded. "Okay. Sorry we suspected you."

50
00:03:57.548 --> 00:04:03.771
"Yeah. And sorry we don't know who you are, even though you're famous," Cole added.

51
00:04:03.772 --> 00:04:09.971
Daniella frowned. "Yes, well, I suppose that's for the best," she said.

52
00:04:09.972 --> 00:04:13.784
"You kids won't give away my secret, will you?"

53
00:04:13.785 --> 00:04:16.793
"Of course not," Cole promised.

54
00:04:16.794 --> 00:04:22.123
Maggie pulled a coin out of her pocket. "Here's your quarter back," she added.

55
00:04:22.124 --> 00:04:24.826
"You never got the lemonade you paid for."

56
00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:29.973
Daniella looked surprised. "Thanks." She took the coin.

57
00:04:29.974 --> 00:04:38.644
"Now I'd better go. I don't want to miss the judging, and it's about to start."

58
00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:42.311
As she hurried off, Henry glanced at the town clock.

59
00:04:42.312 --> 00:04:47.684
"She's right," he said with a sigh. "It's two o'clock."

60
00:04:47.685 --> 00:04:52.669
"We'd better find Nathan and give him the bad news," Cole said.

61
00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.567
"Yeah," Maggie looked hopeful.

62
00:04:55.568 --> 00:05:06.285
"Maybe he found his painting while we were running around chasing Nora and a world-famous artist we never heard of."

63
00:05:06.286 --> 00:05:09.699
But when they found Nathan, he looked sad.

64
00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:15.439
He was staring at the empty spot where his painting had hung.

65
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:20.369
"Oh well," he said when The Lemonade Detectives told him what had happened.

66
00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.254
"I guess I can try again next year.

67
00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:27.001
My painting probably wouldn't have won a prize anyway."

68
00:05:27.002 --> 00:05:28.907
Henry felt terrible.

69
00:05:28.908 --> 00:05:34.255
This was the first case that The Lemonade Detectives had failed to solve.

70
00:05:34.256 --> 00:05:38.457
They all wandered over to the judges, to watch them make their rounds.

71
00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:41.494
The judges were examining Patrick's painting.

72
00:05:41.495 --> 00:05:45.594
"Lovely use of light and shade," the art teacher was saying.

73
00:05:45.595 --> 00:05:52.085
"Indeed," the curator agreed. "Quite accomplished for such a young artist."

74
00:05:52.086 --> 00:05:55.997
Henry looked around to see what Patrick thought of their comments.

75
00:05:55.998 --> 00:05:59.364
To his surprise, Patrick was nowhere in sight.

76
00:05:59.365 --> 00:06:02.779
However, he did notice Hannah watching nearby.

77
00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:06.878
Henry stared from Hannah to Patrick's painting and back again.

78
00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:11.749
"I just remembered something that doesn't quite make sense," he told his friends.

79
00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.772
"Hurry—let's go check it out!"
